From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ryan Murray <ryan@aurorasilicon.org>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 11:48:08 +1100
Subject: [PATCH] ASoC: apple: macaudio: Refuse playback starts after a failed
 speaker lock

When a speaker volume lock fails, prepares are refused and the stop
work moves every running playback stream to XRUN. A stream whose
prepare passed just before the failure was recorded, and which was not
yet PREPARED when the stop work walked the card, could still be
started. Refuse START, RESUME and PAUSE_RELEASE of any playback stream
in the front-end trigger once the lock has failed.

The stop walk also visited back-end runtimes, whose substream shares
the front-end's runtime. That was only harmless because the front-end
links come first in the card's list. Skip no_pcm links there.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Ryan Murray <ryan@aurorasilicon.org>
(cherry picked from commit 2b490ed63cc7a59879e08cb034848c73ce424b18)
Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
---
 sound/soc/apple/macaudio.c | 19 ++++++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 18 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/sound/soc/apple/macaudio.c b/sound/soc/apple/macaudio.c
index 99b79bf733..cc1123e10f 100644
--- a/sound/soc/apple/macaudio.c
+++ b/sound/soc/apple/macaudio.c
@@ -406,7 +406,8 @@ static void macaudio_stop_playback(struct macaudio_snd_data *ma, bool sw_gain_on
 	 * substream on the card carries a runtime as its private data.
 	 */
 	for_each_card_rtds(&ma->card, rtd) {
-		if (!rtd->pcm)
+		/* A back-end's substream shares its front-end's runtime: stop front-ends only. */
+		if (!rtd->pcm || rtd->dai_link->no_pcm)
 			continue;
 		if (sw_gain_only && !ma->link_props[rtd->dai_link->id].sw_gain)
 			continue;
@@ -1272,6 +1273,22 @@ static int macaudio_fe_trigger(struct snd_pcm_substream *substream, int cmd)
 	struct snd_soc_pcm_runtime *rtd = snd_soc_substream_to_rtd(substream);
 	struct macaudio_snd_data *ma = snd_soc_card_get_drvdata(rtd->card);
 
+	/*
+	 * A prepare can pass just before a failed lock is recorded and the
+	 * stop work then find the stream not yet prepared: refuse its start.
+	 */
+	if (substream->stream == SNDRV_PCM_STREAM_PLAYBACK &&
+	    READ_ONCE(ma->speaker_lock_failed)) {
+		switch (cmd) {
+		case SNDRV_PCM_TRIGGER_START:
+		case SNDRV_PCM_TRIGGER_RESUME:
+		case SNDRV_PCM_TRIGGER_PAUSE_RELEASE:
+			return -EIO;
+		default:
+			break;
+		}
+	}
+
 	if (!macaudio_sw_gain_pcm(substream))
 		return 0;
 
